import json,sys
n=sys.argv[1]; out=sys.argv[2]
G="""The twelve are all ALBERTA (Canada). FIRST read every file in /home/andrew/Dev/campgrounds/audit/verify/kit/ab/ (what earlier Alberta batches learned: albertaparks.ca and shop.albertaparks.ca with its cookie jar, Campspot, Let's Camp, Firefly, Checkfront, Cloudbeds, Parks Canada, Wayback for Cloudflare-walled operator sites, the helper scripts in scratchpad p3-371/ .. p3-375/ which you may copy) and keep your own notes file in your scratch directory with anything new. Other verifiers are running at the same time on other batches: use only your own scratch directory, and respect the headless-browser flock. CANADA RULES: every money figure is in Canadian dollars - write fees with the schema's CAD marker (never convert); the private price gate is C$69 base nightly rate for a 23-ft motorhome, mandatory per-person or grounds fees included (flag, do not drop; say whether a major park gateway such as Banff/Canmore/Jasper/Waterton is within 40 km); ownership values are `provincial` (Alberta Parks), `federal` (Parks Canada only), `local` (town, village, county, MD, or a Lions/Rotary club running a campground on municipal land) and `private`. LOOK IT UP, DON'T FLAG IT (owner 2026-11-10): where an entry would clearly stay or go given one more fact you can find with an easy lookup - the entry's stored `rating` group (RV Life price tier and stars), RV Life's index, Google review count and phone, a booking-engine probe - fetch it and report the outcome instead of raising a question; flag only what no lookup settles. A PRIVATE park needs a price indicator (a posted rate, an active booking engine, or RV Life $/$$ - $$$ does not count) and a presence indicator (a working website with a phone, or Google open with 25+ reviews and a phone); the five long-stay tests apply (nights really for sale with no application/lease/waitlist, no standing minimum over 2 nights, at least 1 site in 10 sold nightly, not a home community); workforce and seasonal parks are common in Alberta - measure the nightly share. ALBERTA PARKS entries: read each campground's own albertaparks.ca camping page (not the park root - give its URL), its advisories, and shop.albertaparks.ca; give 2026 season dates (and the shop's 'Closed through' date for 2027), reservable versus first-come, rates by site type, power/water/sewer by loop with amperage, maximum unit length, site count, facilities, winter camping, and the 'Facility Operator' and 'Information' phone lines (stored phones are often empty). The `provincial:AB` policy row holds the booking window, reservation fee and standard discounts - do not repeat them per entry; report contradictions and which pages carry the 'Alberta seniors' discount line; a campground leased to a municipality and booked outside shop.albertaparks.ca may need policy_ref none (report it). LOCAL entries: rates, season, booking channel and phone from the municipality's or operator's own page. WATERFRONT (confirm, log a lead, or recommend a downgrade; never upgrade): within about 50 m of the water with only open ground between; a few clearly waterfront sites count if named. Earlier Alberta batches downgraded nine of twenty stored waterfront values (trees on the bank, marsh, shoreline trails, drawdown flats, a road, a lagoon that is not a lake). For every entry beside water say how far the nearest sites are and what lies between. Read the pin against imagery for all twelve and report one more than about 250 m off the campsites with corrected coordinates (earlier batches found pins on a visitor centre, a cemetery, and one 111 km off). FOUND IN EARLIER ALBERTA BATCHES: no drops; many empty or wrong phones; first-come campgrounds stored as reservable; a stored C$10 rate that was a cook-house fee; Lions campgrounds stored private that are town-owned; dead or hijacked old domains (never cite one).
THIS BATCH:"""
L=[]
for d in json.load(open(f'/home/andrew/Dev/campgrounds/audit/verify/batches/p3-{n}.json')):
    e=d['entry']; r=e.get('rating') or {}; f=(e.get('fees') or {}).get('nightly_low'); o=e.get('ownership'); w=e.get('waterfront')
    s=[f"{e['id']} {e['name']} ({o}"]
    s[0]+=f", stored {w}" if w!='not waterfront' else ''
    s[0]+=f", stored C${f}" if f is not None else ', no rate stored'
    s[0]+=f", RV Life {'$'*(r.get('price_tier') or 0) or 'none'}" if o=='private' else ''
    s[0]+=', no phone stored' if not e.get('phone') else ''
    s[0]+=')'
    x=[]
    if w not in ('not waterfront',None): x.append(f'check the stored {w} value hard')
    if o=='private':
        if f is None: x.append('find a posted nightly rate or engine quote')
        elif f>69: x.append('stored rate is over the C$69 gate - confirm the base rate for a 23-ft rig and any gateway')
        elif f>=55: x.append('rate is near the gate - confirm a dated base rate')
        x.append('long-stay tests')
    if o=='provincial' and e.get('website','').split('\n')[0].rstrip('/').count('/')<=5: x.append('website is the park root - give the camping page')
    if 'koa' in e['name'].lower(): x.append('KOA: price with koa.py as for any private park')
    L.append(s[0]+(': '+'; '.join(x) if x else ''))
open(out,'w').write(G+' '+'. '.join(L)+'.\n')
